  "notes": "{掴|つか}む is a transitive verb meaning to grab or grasp firmly, both physically and figuratively.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pattern: 〜を{掴|つか}む\n\nPHYSICAL GRASPING:\n- {手|て}を{掴|つか}む: to grab someone's hand\n- ロープを{掴|つか}む: to grab a rope\n- {襟|えり}を{掴|つか}む: to grab by the collar\n\nFIGURATIVE USE:\n- チャンスを{掴|つか}む: to seize an opportunity\n- {心|こころ}を{掴|つか}む: to capture someone's heart\n- {要点|ようてん}を{掴|つか}む: to grasp the main point\n- {成功|せいこう}を{掴|つか}む: to achieve success\n\nSIMILAR VERBS:\n- {握|にぎ}る: to grip, hold (sustained holding)\n- {取|と}る: to take (more general)\n- {捕|つか}まえる: to catch, capture (person/animal)",
